course: dictionary
lesson: 6558
title: Nibble: a small bite
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Nibble most often means to eat something by taking very small bites. «Rats are cautious with new food: they nibble a little and wait to see whether they feel ill.» The rat takes tiny bites, so nibble means small bites.
explain: Look at the words around nibble. «A fish nibbled my toe» and «a nibble on the line» are about fishing: the fish is gently biting, not really eating. «Nibbles and drinks» at a party means small snacks, like crisps and nuts. The subject of the sentence and the place tell you the meaning.
explain: Nibble can be a verb or a noun. «Goats nibble a bit of everything» uses the verb: the goats are doing the nibbling. «Take a nibble» uses the noun: it means one small bite. To check, swap in your meaning: if «a small bite» fits the sentence, you have it.
fact: Nibble means to take very small bites of something.
fact: Animals such as mice, rabbits and hamsters nibble with their sharp front teeth.
fact: «Nibbled» means bitten in small bits, as in «nibbled edges» on a leaf.
fact: A nibble can also be a gentle bite, like «a fish nibbled my toe», or a small bite of food, as in «take a nibble».
fact: «Nibbles» in the plural means small snacks at a party, like crisps and nuts, in British English.
exercise: «Rats are cautious with new food: they nibble a little and wait to see whether they feel ill.» What does nibble mean here? | To hide food under the bed | To swallow with a loud crunch | *To take very small bites | To gobble everything up in one go
exercise: «A fish nibbled my toe.» What is the fish doing? | *Biting gently | Singing a song | Eating the whole toe | Swimming very fast
exercise: «Take a nibble of my cake.» Find and copy the word that means one small bite. | cake | take | my | *nibble
test: «There were nibbles and drinks at the party.» What are nibbles? | Drinks in glass bottles | Toys for the children | Large dinners for the whole family | *Small snacks, like crisps and nuts
test: «The satanic leaf-tailed gecko has nibbled edges.» What does nibbled mean? | Cut in a perfectly straight line | *Bitten in small bits | Painted in bright colours | Blown away by the wind
exam: «Goats nibble a bit of everything, but they do not really eat tin cans.» Which word tells you what the goats are doing? | Goats | Everything | *Nibble | Tin
